---
import LegalShell from "../components/LegalShell.astro"
---

<LegalShell title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using Blesser to find and track opportunities.">
  <section>
    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      Blesser lists grants, accelerators, fellowships, scholarships and other opportunities, and helps you track your applications,
      to-dos and deadlines. Listings are found by automated agents and by people, and can be wrong or out of date: always check the
      official page before you apply or rely on a deadline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep your sign-in details safe.</li>
      <li>Only share real opportunities, with a link to their official page.</li>
      <li>Don't use Blesser to send spam, to harass anyone, or to overload the service.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time in Settings. We may suspend accounts that break these terms or put the service at risk.
      See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a> for how your data is handled.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalShell>
